    <div class="rich"><p>If your well pump is clicking on and off every few seconds, you probably need pressure tank replacement in Wenatchee, not a new pump. The pressure tank is the cheapest part of your well system to fix, and the most expensive one to ignore. A bad tank makes your pump cycle constantly, and that wears out a $2,500 pump to protect a $600 tank.</p><p>Wenatchee Well Pros services and replaces pressure tanks across Chelan, Douglas, and Grant counties. Most replacements run $600 to $1,800 installed, and most are done in a single visit. Call <strong>(509) 351-8404</strong> for a free estimate, or keep reading to see if your tank is the real problem.</p></div>
